SPEC.md §9.4, DECISIONS 296, 456: a ref into a keyed list is not a finite type, so a function taking one is translated, and E9006 refuses it, a package fn and a record's method alike; only a ref into a table is finite.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A row.
record Row {
  /// Its key.
  id: String
}

/// The rows.
let rows: [Row] keyed by id = [ { id: "x" } ]

/// A holder.
record Holder {
  /// Its weight.
  w: Int
  /// A method over a ref into a keyed list.
  export fn at(self, x: ref rows) -> Int { return self.w }
}

/// Pick, whatever x.
export fn pick(x: ref rows, b: Bool) -> Int { return if b { 1 } else { 0 } }

emit go { out: "@features/a", package: "a" }
-- findings.txt --
error[E9006]  a/a.canon:17:22
  parameter x of Holder.at has type ref a.rows: translated functions take Bool, integers, Float, Float32, String, Duration and enums; pass the values the body reads as parameters of those types, or make Holder.at a method of the record that holds them

error[E9006]  a/a.canon:21:16
  parameter x of pick has type ref a.rows: translated functions take Bool, integers, Float, Float32, String, Duration and enums; pass the values the body reads as parameters of those types, or make pick a method of the record that holds them

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
